<</Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/Alt (The agentlore second brain. Upper lane: working sessions write transcripts; lore index reads what is new, redacts secrets, chunks it and writes index.db; the MCP server reads the index for agents. Lower lane: agents save notes with remember, a Stop hook asks them to, and lore consolidate updates the notes daily from new excerpts; notes live in project memory, are indexed, and reach new sessions through the SessionStart hook; the UserPromptSubmit hook adds related excerpts to each prompt.)
